From 1737c52c9ad4daef3902c484d38d879342daf9c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hoangvu12 <hggaming91@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:06:06 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] engine: boot opens only the journals that changed since they
 were last seen closed

Boot's crash scan (RunJournal::stale_sessions) opened every journal ever
written to read its tail. On Windows an on-access virus scan reads a whole
file before the first open returns, so with a cold scan cache (after a
reboot or a signature update) 1,133 journals (1.1 GB) took 32 s, and the
engine was not ready until it finished: 35-49 s from launch.

A journal is append-only, so one last seen ending in a closed turn whose
size and modified time are unchanged has not changed. closed-journals.idx,
beside the journals, remembers those; boot reads each journal's metadata
(no data opened, so no scan) and opens only the new or changed ones, 8 at
a time, since those scans overlap. Losing the index costs one slower boot;
a wrong line can't hide a crash, since any write changes the length.

Measured on a copy of a real profile with a cold scan cache: 34.6 s before,
1.5 s after; the first boot after the update builds the index in ~11 s.
---
 crates/engine/src/run_journal.rs | 258 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 252 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

